A||||4||Richard Parnell||Question for other V8 Fiero owners||||5||
Z||000000||Richard Parnell||04-16-2001||04:48 PM||||All you guys with V8 Archie kits.  Since we use the archie kit the drive axles are stock.  That being so, the engine sits off center towards the passenger side and the passenger side deck hinge is just fractions of an inch above the front side valve cover.  Does everyone have to drop the cradle to adjust their valves?  Is there something I can do to modify the hinge (to another position maybe)?  I need to adjust my valves and really do not look forward to disconnecting a bunch of stuff and dropping the cradle.  Any comments?||||reg||5
Z||000001||BUCK WILLIAMS||04-16-2001||06:13 PM||||I WATCHED ARCHIE ADJUST THE VALVES ON A V8 GT IN DAYTONA FOR A MAN WITH HIS KIT (VERY NICE CAR)IN IT.  HE REMOVED THE HOOD. THAT GAVE PLENTY OF ROOM! CALL ARCHIE. HE ALWAYS LIKES TO HELP FOLKS WITH HIS KITS!||||reg||7
Z||000002||Richard Parnell||04-16-2001||06:44 PM||||Well duhh.  I never thought about that, though I've heard it's tough to get the springs back into place.  But can't be nearly as tough as dropping the cradle. Ok so I've got moron written on my forehead.||||reg||11
Z||000003||V8Fiero||04-16-2001||06:58 PM||||Well, funny you should ask. I am just trying to get my car up and running. I got it running but had an oil leak from that front valve cover. Like you said. Its about an inch from the hinge. I took a rotary tool and cut back the bottom of the hinge as close to the spring as possible. The cover came off easy and doesnt bother the spring either.....<BR>Hope this helps.<BR>Scott||||reg||1
Z||000004||Formula88||04-17-2001||08:50 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Richard Parnell:<BR><B>Well duhh.  I never thought about that, though I've heard it's tough to get the springs back into place.  But can't be nearly as tough as dropping the cradle. Ok so I've got moron written on my forehead.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Actually, you don't have to worry about the springs on the deck lid.  You just take off 2 bolts on each hinge and lift the lid off of the hinge.  Don't take off the torx style bolt in between the 2 regular bolts on the hinge, because that's the one that connect to the torque bar.  Piece of cake.  <BR>||||reg||6
